{"name":"Valley Floor","hex":"#848d85","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"valley floor","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The lowest part or bottom of a valley (as seen in a cross-section)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/valley_floor"}],"entries":[{"title":"Valley","blocks":[{"text":"A valley is an elongated low area often running between hills or mountains and typically containing a river or stream running from one end to the other. Most valleys are formed by erosion of the land surface by rivers or streams over a very long period. Some valleys are formed through erosion by glacial ice. These glaciers may remain present in valleys in high mountains or polar areas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Salta-VallesCalchaquies-P3140151.JPG/330px-Salta-VallesCalchaquies-P3140151.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley","wikidata":"Q39816"},{"title":"Floor","blocks":[{"text":"A floor is the bottom surface of typically an enclosed space such as a room or vehicle. Floors vary from simple dirt in a cave to many layered surfaces made with modern technology. Floors may be stone, wood, bamboo, metal, or any other material that can support the expected load."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Parquet_flooring_in_Mus%C3%A9e_des_arts_d%C3%A9coratifs_de_Strasbourg.jpg/330px-Parquet_flooring_in_Mus%C3%A9e_des_arts_d%C3%A9coratifs_de_Strasbourg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Floor","wikidata":"Q217164"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Glacier_park1.jpg/500px-Glacier_park1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Glacier_park1.jpg/1280px-Glacier_park1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikip